  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namati is a global network of grassroots legal advocates working with local communities to understand, use, and shape the law in order to gain access to basic services and rights. Since its founding in 2012, Namati has built a global movement of community paralegals to advance justice in multiple sectors. Namati has trained and deployed over 400 community paralegals who have taken up over 40,000 justice issues with local communities and contributed to case wins that have directly improved the lives of at least 1.3 million people. Over the next two years, Namati will continue to pursue systemic change in six countries while growing the global Legal Empowerment Network advocacy influence. (Strategy: Inclusive Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
